From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nirmoy Das <nirmoyd@nvidia.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Feb 2026 08:26:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: SAUCE: vfio: Remove vfio_device_from_file()
 declaration

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2138892

Remove this declaration which is now used within the file
after merging upstream "vfio/nvgrace-gpu: register device memory for
poison handling".

Signed-off-by: Nirmoy Das <nirmoyd@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Matthew R. Ochs <mochs@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Jamie Nguyen <jamien@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Brad Figg <bfigg@nvidia.com>
Ledger-Change: C-00419
Ledger-Origin: nvidia-6.17@a7a81868a75e22baf2182507776bb8b0dfc5f39d
---
 include/linux/vfio.h | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/linux/vfio.h b/include/linux/vfio.h
index 62e67f73a909..eb563f538dee 100644
--- a/include/linux/vfio.h
+++ b/include/linux/vfio.h
@@ -331,7 +331,6 @@ static inline bool vfio_file_has_dev(struct file *file, struct vfio_device *devi
 	return false;
 }
 #endif
-struct vfio_device *vfio_device_from_file(struct file *file);
 bool vfio_file_is_valid(struct file *file);
 bool vfio_file_enforced_coherent(struct file *file);
 void vfio_file_set_kvm(struct file *file, struct kvm *kvm);
